# Vercel Web Analytics Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js project.

## Implementation Details

### 1. Documentation Review
- Fetched the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
- Identified Next.js App Router as the framework in use
- Confirmed the correct installation approach for this project

### 2. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 using npm
- Package added to dependencies in package.json
- Updated package-lock.json to ensure consistent dependency resolution

### 3. Configuration
The Analytics component was already properly configured in the codebase:
- Location: `app/layout.tsx` (root layout)
- Import: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
- Placement: Component placed at the end of the `<body>` tag, following Next.js App Router best practices
- The implementation matches the official Vercel documentation exactly

### 4. Testing & Verification
✅ Build test: Passed successfully (`npm run build`)
- Production build completed without errors
- 24 routes generated successfully
- TypeScript compilation completed successfully

✅ Linter check: Pre-existing warnings/errors unrelated to this change
- The Analytics implementation introduces no new linting issues
- Existing issues are in unrelated components (SeriesCarousel, ArchivoPlctoricoSection)

## Files Modified
- `package.json` - Added `@vercel/analytics` to dependencies
- `package-lock.json` - Updated with new package and its dependencies

## Files Staged for Commit
- package.json
- package-lock.json

## Next Steps
To activate Web Analytics:
1. Deploy this project to Vercel
2. Enable Web Analytics in your Vercel dashboard under the Analytics tab
3. Analytics will begin tracking page views automatically after deployment

## Notes
- The Analytics component was already imported and placed in the layout.tsx file, but the package itself was not installed in node_modules
- This installation completes the setup by adding the missing dependency
- The implementation follows the official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router
- No code changes were needed as the configuration was already correct
